# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-11, 2.1-18, C-4). L §5.14: "A hole in a term (an attribute that is a hole ...) makes the
# arcs it ranks undecided. Only the parts the take could reach under some reading of the holes merge, into one hole part
# with the total known"; "A fill refuses an undecided order (RUN-ORDER) ...; a take's outcome is a fact, so it stays a
# hole". w1's paid_from is a hole: either part could go first, so ania's 100.00 and tomek's 50.00 merge into one hole
# part of 120.00 that may be either's (HOLE-PART), the total 120.00 known, and w1's leg read of tomek a hole too.
# L5_14_parts_decided answers the hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if w in withdrawals and k.owner == w.paid_from then 0 else 1
kind withdrawals: transfers
  attr paid_from: key persons
kind tomeks: transfers
input pf: key persons
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
input w1_day: date
input w1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount t1_amt
move w1: withdrawals
  on w1_day
  attr paid_from = pf
  leg cash from konto to shop amount w1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, w1.cash.amount of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 50.00 PLN
  w1_day = 2026-03-01
  w1_amt = 30.00 PLN
  pf = ?"who paid"
=== expect
q: (120.00 PLN, ?"konto: 120.00 PLN may be ania's: who paid" (konto), ?"konto: 120.00 PLN may be tomek's: who paid" (konto), ?"konto: 30.00 PLN may be tomek's: who paid" (konto))
  cut 2026-01-01
